      "question": "Solve only the current attached TASK.md or visible LeetCode task. Start with the exact context marker from that attachment. Then give a single fenced javascript block defining function solve with the specified arguments and return value, with no imports or exports. Include complete runnable implementation, then state time and space complexity. Do not use prior tasks.",
      "answer": "CTX-1-c82dfd3d8e7f\n\n```javascript\nfunction solve(nums1, nums2) {\n  if (nums1.length > nums2.length) {\n    [nums1, nums2] = [nums2, nums1];\n  }\n\n  const m = nums1.length;\n  const n = nums2.length;\n  const leftSize = Math.floor((m + n + 1) / 2);\n  let low = 0;\n  let high = m;\n\n  while (low <= high) {\n    const i = Math.floor((low + high) / 2);\n    const j = leftSize - i;\n\n    const aLeft = i === 0 ? -Infinity : nums1[i - 1];\n    const aRight = i === m ? Infinity : nums1[i];\n    const bLeft = j === 0 ? -Infinity : nums2[j - 1];\n    const bRight = j === n ? Infinity : nums2[j];\n\n    if (aLeft <= bRight && bLeft <= aRight) {\n      const leftMax = Math.max(aLeft, bLeft);\n      if ((m + n) % 2 === 1) return leftMax;\n      return (leftMax + Math.min(aRight, bRight)) / 2;\n    }\n\n    if (aLeft > bRight) {\n      high = i - 1;\n    } else {\n      low = i + 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  throw new Error('Inputs must be sorted in ascending order.');\n}\n```\n\nTime: O(log(min(m, n) + 1)), within the O(log(m + n)) target. Space: O(1).",
