      "question": "Solve only the current attached TASK.md or visible LeetCode task. Start with the exact context marker from that attachment. Then give a single fenced javascript block defining function solve with the specified arguments and return value, with no imports or exports. Include complete runnable implementation, then state time and space complexity. Do not use prior tasks.",
      "answer": "CTX-2-96a485782bae\n\n```javascript\nfunction solve(s, p) {\n  const m = s.length;\n  const n = p.length;\n  let prev = new Array(n + 1).fill(false);\n  prev[0] = true;\n\n  for (let j = 2; j <= n; j++) {\n    if (p[j - 1] === '*') prev[j] = prev[j - 2];\n  }\n\n  for (let i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\n    const curr = new Array(n + 1).fill(false);\n    for (let j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n      if (p[j - 1] === '*') {\n        const atom = p[j - 2];\n        const matches = atom === '.' || atom === s[i - 1];\n        curr[j] = curr[j - 2] || (matches && prev[j]);\n      } else {\n        const matches = p[j - 1] === '.' || p[j - 1] === s[i - 1];\n        curr[j] = matches && prev[j - 1];\n      }\n    }\n    prev = curr;\n  }\n\n  return prev[n];\n}\n```\n\nTime: O((|s| + 1)(|p| + 1)). Space: O(|p| + 1).",
